The template `GetBitsSignedValueT` isn't visible here, so this rewrite assumes it returns the unsigned bit-field value sign-extended from `bits`. I haven't compiled or tested it. Edge cases (`bits == 0` or `bits >= 64`) fall back to the original template call, so their behavior is unchanged. Please verify against the decode test corpus before relying on it.

```cpp
FIT_SINT64 FieldBase::GetBitsSignedValue64(const FIT_UINT16 offset, const FIT_UINT8 bits) const
{
    if (bits == 0 || bits >= 64)
    {
        return GetBitsSignedValueT<FIT_SINT64>(offset, bits);
    }
    const FIT_UINT64 raw = static_cast<FIT_UINT64>(GetBitsValue64(offset, bits));
    const FIT_UINT64 signBit = static_cast<FIT_UINT64>(1) << (bits - 1);
    const FIT_UINT64 mask = (static_cast<FIT_UINT64>(1) << bits) - 1;
    const FIT_UINT64 v = raw & mask;
    return static_cast<FIT_SINT64>((v ^ signBit) - signBit);
}
```